WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.791
The full assessment covers eight areas,
run in a fixed order: forest topology,

2
00:00:06.791 --> 00:00:13.638
the OU hierarchy, Group Policy, DNS, AD CS,
computers, users and groups, and trusts.

3
00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:17.537
Most of the forest is readable
by any authenticated user.

4
00:00:17.537 --> 00:00:20.669
The parts that aren't are
the reason Chapter 08 exists,

5
00:00:20.669 --> 00:00:24.013
so each collector runs on the
narrowest right that works.

6
00:00:24.013 --> 00:00:28.865
Topology, computers, and users and
groups need only an authenticated user;

7
00:00:28.865 --> 00:00:32.048
delegation attributes
are readable by default,

8
00:00:32.048 --> 00:00:35.787
though recursive group expansion
is slow in big forests.

9
00:00:35.787 --> 00:00:40.389
The OU collector needs read permission
on the OUs' security descriptors,

10
00:00:40.389 --> 00:00:43.226
because some ACLs aren't
readable by default.

11
00:00:43.226 --> 00:00:46.176
Group Policy needs read
on the GPOs and SYSVOL,

12
00:00:46.176 --> 00:00:50.525
plus the backup right through
Group Policy Management delegation.

13
00:00:50.525 --> 00:00:55.700
DNS needs read on each DNS server,
delegated on the server object.

14
00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.888
AD CS needs read on the Public Key
Services containers and on each CA.

15
00:01:00.888 --> 00:01:03.005
And trusts: any user can list them,

16
00:01:03.005 --> 00:01:06.925
but verification needs domain
administrator credentials.

17
00:01:06.925 --> 00:01:09.875
Two rights the source design
asked for are refused.

18
00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:15.592
DnsAdmins: Microsoft treats it as privileged,
because its members control the DNS

19
00:01:15.592 --> 00:01:21.225
Server service, and Defender for Identity
flags non-privileged members as a risk.

20
00:01:21.225 --> 00:01:25.600
Grant read on the DNS server object
to a dedicated group instead.

21
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.425
And standing Domain Admin:
no assessment run uses one.

22
00:01:29.425 --> 00:01:33.290
Trust verification is the only
step that needs those rights,

23
00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.613
and it runs separately under
just-in-time elevation.

24
00:01:36.613 --> 00:01:41.930
The host is a domain-joined Windows
Server 2025 or Windows 11 machine

25
00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:47.249
with the Remote Server Administration
Tools, at build 26100 or later.

26
00:01:47.249 --> 00:01:50.372
The account is a group
managed service account,

27
00:01:50.372 --> 00:01:54.775
with delegated read and nothing
more, so no password is ever stored.

28
00:01:54.775 --> 00:01:56.697
Two corrections from review:

29
00:01:56.697 --> 00:02:01.904
the AD CS administration module the source
required isn't used by any function,

30
00:02:01.904 --> 00:02:04.307
and the PSPKI module is now optional,

31
00:02:04.307 --> 00:02:07.970
because its publisher no
longer actively supports it.
